{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_015Pts6X6PepKzxYjCBnqhf6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **Q19 — Success metrics for an ML model?** is written and committed.\n\nThe note covers:\n\n- **Three-layer framework**: task-appropriate offline metrics → calibration → business KPI\n- **Offline metrics table** by task type: PR-AUC for imbalanced classification, NDCG/MRR for ranking, RAGAS Faithfulness/Answer Relevancy for generative LLM, MAE/RMSE for regression\n- **Calibration layer**: Expected Calibration Error (ECE), reliability diagrams, Platt scaling — the silent failure mode most candidates skip entirely\n- **Business KPI mapping**: deflection rate for chatbots, dollar-loss-prevented for fraud, revenue lift for recommenders — with A/B testing as the validation bridge\n- **Two concrete tradeoff examples**: fraud model where the business-optimal threshold (0.23) diverged from the default (0.50) due to miscalibration; LLM chatbot where Faithfulness looked fine but deflection rate was low because answers were too verbose\n- **Pitfall on accuracy for imbalanced data** — a concrete reason interviewers ask this (99% accuracy on 1% positive-rate = useless)\n\nNext up: **Q20 — A/B testing for prompt variations?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_read_input_tokens":69465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":88,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b0a6cdc-eb7b-4f82-9e63-3b896a4aa3c6","uuid":"ee34d776-668c-4cf1-9676-858adfd6114e"}
